            "node_id": "zm.aic.agent.deep_reasoning",
            "reference_id": "dp1",
            "node_type": "deep_reasoning",
            "node_name": "AI reasoning",
            "node_alias": "",
            "node_desc": "",
            "input_map": {
              "task_prompt": "# Execution contract\n\n## Role\nMeeting reminder assistant\n\n## Objective\nSend the workflow owner a Slack direct message with the essentials of their meeting that starts in 15 minutes.\n\n## Requested delivery action\nsend\n\n## Inputs\n- **meeting** from `{{trg1.meeting}}` — The upcoming meeting from the trigger: its topic, meeting number, and invitees, and the key for the Zoom Meetings lookup\n\n## Procedure\n1. Look up the meeting with Zoom Meetings by its meeting number or ID and read its scheduled start time and time zone, duration, passcode, host, invitees, agenda or description, and join link; use the trigger's meeting fields when the lookup does not return a value.\n2. Compose the meeting essentials from the meeting in this structure: MEETING OVERVIEW (topic; start time as 'Day, Month DD at H:MM AM/PM' with its time zone; duration; meeting ID; passcode if available; host), INVITEES (every invitee by name), AGENDA (numbered agenda topics, with time allocation when stated), PREPARATION CHECKLIST (documents to review, materials to prepare, pre-meeting tasks, technical setup), JOIN INFORMATION (the meeting link).\n3. Find the workflow owner's Slack user by their email, then send the essentials once as a Slack direct message in mrkdwn, opening with the meeting topic and that it starts in 15 minutes. List invitees by name without mentions.\n\n## Output requirements\n- Return the delivered reminder text and the provider-confirmed delivery status.\n\n## Typed outputs\n- `response` (string): Plain-language execution result, including observed side-effect status when applicable\n\n## Missing-data policy\nWrite 'Not stated' for any field the meeting does not provide, and leave the preparation checklist to what the meeting's agenda or description supports; never invent items. If the workflow owner has no Slack user with their email, stop without sending and report it.\n\n## Evidence policy\nUse only the trigger's meeting and what the Zoom Meetings lookup returns for that meeting.\n\n## Tool policy\nUse Zoom Meetings only to read this meeting's details, and only Slack to deliver.\n\n## Side-effect policy\nSend exactly one direct message to the workflow owner and report success only after Slack confirms it.\n\n## Success criteria\n- Every stated fact comes from the meeting.\n- The delivery output reflects the observed provider result.\n\n## Execution receipt\n- Begin the `response` value with a compact execution receipt of at most 1000 characters, before any report, message body, analysis, or other long-form content.\n- Start the receipt with `Outcome: SUCCESS`, `Outcome: PARTIAL`, `Outcome: NO_ACTION`, or `Outcome: FAILED`, matching the observed run result.\n- Add `Reads:` with the provider/source plus the concrete record identifiers, titles, queries, or result counts actually observed and used; write `Reads: NONE` when no read ran.\n- Add `Writes:` with one compact entry per attempted side effect: provider, operation, resolved target or recipient, provider-confirmed status, and returned identifier or URL when the tool supplies one. If no write ran, state `Writes: NONE` and the reason.\n- Add `Checks:` with every core requested section, field, constraint, and required sink marked `OK` or `MISSING` from observed evidence. Keep it terse, but never omit a failed core check to fit the receipt; for a long artifact, this checklist is the bounded proof of its contents.\n- Never claim success from intent or generated content alone, never invent receipt evidence, and never defer the only business-outcome evidence until after long-form content.",
              "system_prompt": "",
              "max_steps": 20,
              "knowledge": {
                "web_urls": ""
